      ],
      "message": "memusage: Make fields of STL helper structs public\n\nThe `stl_tree_node`, `list_node` and `unordered_node` class templates\nonly mimic the layout of the standard library's container nodes, so\nthat `sizeof` yields an estimate of the memory they use. Their fields\nare never accessed.\n\nSince llvm/llvm-project#237374, Clang 24 diagnoses these fields with\n`-Wunused-private-field`.\n\nThis change drops the `private:` access specifiers. It does not affect\nthe size or alignment of the structs, as all their fields keep the same\naccess control, and it is consistent with `stl_shared_counter`.",
